ng authorization for tests and side effects. An unchecked deployment\012  or live-provider gate does not itself authorize publication or spending.\012- Do not use subagents. Use Git only inside the applicable repositories.\012\012Update the tracking file and stop this invocation:\012\012- Maintain - [ ] for incomplete gates and - [x] only for gates whose stated\012  acceptance criteria passed. Preserve IDs, unresolved criteria and dated failures.\012- Maintain compact Checked-item evidence only for acceptance gates whose current\012  state matters: ID, implemented/verified/deployed state, a short evidence reference,\012  and last relevant change. Do not accumulate one prose log entry per iteration.\012  If new evidence invalidates a checked item, reopen it with the current reason;\012  the runner-owned archive retains earlier snapshots.\012- Replace Current handoff near the top with: active checkbox, criteria closed this\012  iteration, remaining criteria, blocker/dependency, concise verification results\012  including skips, deferred gates with unblock conditions, and the exact next ready\012  checkbox. Delete superseded handoff prose rather than moving it into a history\012  section. Continue the unfinished active gate unless its documented blocker makes\012  another gate ready.\012- Keep timing and exit information concise in the current handoff: approximate\012  discovery/implementation/verification durations when useful, loaded prompt\012  revision, declared batch outcome and exit reason. Do not create a growing dated\012  iteration-history section; the runner archives each boundary snapshot separately.\012  If exiting early with an unfinished outcome, explain only the current reason.\012- Summarize concrete changes and checks; explain any scope change. If no gate\012  closed, identify the material prerequisite advanced and how it reduces the\012  remaining work. Repeated rediscovery, extra notes or adjacent tests alone\012  are not progress toward the active gate.\012- Treat blockers as **gate-local deferrals**, not as a reason to end the long-running\012  executor. When a gate cannot advance, record its blocker, evidence, unblock\012  condition and a bounded retry trigger, then SKIP it and scan every other unchecked\012  gate for useful authorized implementation, repair, investigation or verification.\012  Do not repeatedly spend fresh sessions on an unchanged blocker or failed check.\012- If Runner context says Blocked recovery mode: YES, the previous session exhausted\012  its ready set. Re-evaluate dependency facts once, then actively seek an alternative:\012  another ready gate, an independent child, preparatory work that reduces a blocker,\012  or a newly feasible verification/repair. Replace stale handoff targets rather than\012  retrying the same stuck action merely because it was previously active.\012- In the bounded `## Deferred gates` section, flag each problematic task using one\012  line: `- BLOCKED TASK-ID: reason | Unblock: exact condition | Retry: trigger`,\012  `- NEEDS_INFO TASK-ID: question | Unblock: required answer | Retry: answer arrives`,\012  `- PROBLEM TASK-ID: failed check | Unblock: repair | Retry: changed evidence`, or\012  `- SKIPPED TASK-ID: dependency | Unblock: prerequisite | Retry: prerequisite done`.\012  Keep these task IDs stable, remove the flag when resolved, and leave the task's\012  acceptance checkbox unchecked until implementation and validation both pass.\012  A deferral is visible unfinished work. Prefer independent ready tasks over a\012  repeated attempt on unchanged blockers; ask one precise question when input is needed.\012- Status: BLOCKED is a **non-terminal recovery signal**. Use it only when this\012  session finds no materially useful authorized action after scanning ALL remaining\012  gates and prerequisites. Record every blocking dependency and exact external\012  unblock action. The runner will start another fresh recovery worker rather than\012  exit. Prefer Status: IN_PROGRESS whenever any useful work can advance.\012- Set Status: COMPLETE only when every original gate and its required in-scope\012  follow-up/child checkboxes are implemented and verified. New children must neither\012  broaden original scope nor hide unfinished original acceptance criteria.\012  Otherwise use Status: IN_PROGRESS when material progress permits continuation.\012  Maintain exactly one of these status lines in the tracking file opening header, after an\012  optional # title and before the first ## (or deeper) section heading, outside\012  code fences. Historical status lines belong in sections below the header.\012\012When Runner context says Recovery verification required: YES, re-evaluate the\012persisted terminal status and acceptance evidence before trusting prior completion.\012The last session may have failed, timed out or exhausted quota after editing state.\012Preserve proven work and flags, validate remaining criteria, then continue ready tasks.\012\012\012Runner context:\012Runner role: WORKER\012Source roadmap snapshot: "/Users/bpstr/Github/edit-ac/architecture/progress/.roadmap-runner/03-local-storage-490e984e7714/source-4b0b018a0077.md"\012Source roadmap revision: de87af3a7d5686a655adf8e338854b0130467cf14d2056652f4c979f6eab7e95\012Roadmap reconciliation required: NO\012Use this read-only snapshot for all source requirements in this session, not the changing live file.\012An external controller may revise the live roadmap; adopt later revisions only on the next run.\012Neither workers nor the periodic supervisor may edit the live source or snapshot, weaken criteria, or expand permissions/budgets.\012Recovery verification required: NO\012Blocked recovery mode: NO\012Loaded prompt revision: 7eaa063f3629\012Iteration: 1\012Session started (UTC): 2026-10-12T07:46:17.657Z\012
